# inference-api-key-auth.j2 teaches API-key auth at an inference gateway. Its
# verification step deliberately sends an unregistered key to demonstrate a
# 401/403 response. gitleaks' curl-auth-header rule flags any value in an
# X-Api-Key header, so the original literal ("WRONG_KEY", added in the commit
# below) is a training placeholder, not a real secret. The template now uses a
# shell variable ($INVALID_KEY) instead; this entry suppresses the historical
# finding so the PR range scan stays green. Refs #567.
